KZ3 patch 2144 (RSX pass 133): a draw that samples its own render target reads it even when other surfaces share the address.
Design and code from the Killzone 2 port (its patch 2097); both projects are MIT and have the same owner.

Symptom (Killzone 2, pause menu): the whole screen went white. The colour grade draws into a target and samples that same
target (same address and size); the texture-to-surface lookup skips the bound target and takes the best other surface at
the address, and only when there is none falls back to the target's feedback copy. With another surface sharing the
address (the pause screen's composite) the grade read last frame's picture and graded it again every frame.
Killzone 3 has the same lookup (sink_end_impl texture loop: "i == target" is skipped, feedback only when sampled < 0).

Fix: a texture whose address and size are the bound target's is a self-read and takes the feedback copy whatever else
shares the address. Other aliases keep the old rule. "[self-read]" logs the first redirections. LD_NO_SELF_EXACT=1 = old.
Host test: none (the rule sits in the walker's bind loop). Upstream candidate.

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
--- a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c	2026-11-02 15:28:45.340388901 -0600
